# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# NOTE: intentionally NOT ignored (the Dockerfile COPYs them or CI needs them):
#   .git                 -> "COPY .git .git" (git describe/rev-parse ldflags)
#   docker-bin/          -> prebuilt binaries (BINARY_SOURCE=prebuilt)
#   cmd/, pkg/           -> Go bridge sources
#   SteamBridge/         -> C# service sources (only bin/ and obj/ below are out)
#   go.mod, go.sum       -> "COPY go.mod go.sum ./" + go mod download layer
#   entrypoint.sh        -> copied into the runtime image

# .NET build output (would otherwise defeat the "COPY SteamBridge/" cache layer
# and, worse, ship stale host-built binaries)
SteamBridge/bin/
SteamBridge/obj/

# Local runtime junk / reference tree / CI metadata
logs/
ref/
.github/
.mcp.json

# Archives sometimes dropped next to the Dockerfile by CI packaging steps
*.tar.gz
*.zip
